Sources of the real (off-air) recordings in this directory. All other WAV
files here are generated by tools/gen_test_wavs.py or are decoder output
references and are covered by the repository licence.

real_aprs_wa8lmf_30s.wav
  First 30 s of Track 1 of the "TNC Test CD" by
  WA8LMF, http://www.wa8lmf.net/TNCtest . Off-air 144.39 MHz APRS, Los Angeles,
  2005. The source describes the CD as freely distributed; no explicit
  open-source licence was found. TODO: confirm redistribution terms with the
  author or replace with a self-recorded clip.

real_pocsag_1200_taunus.wav
  First 12 s of "POCSAG-1200.WAV" from
  http://www.signals.taunus.de/WAV/POCSAG.HTML . Off-air recording of a German
  pager network. No licence statement was found on the source page.
  TODO: confirm redistribution terms with the site owner or replace.

real_sstv_ariss_series34_robot36.wav
  42 s excerpt of an off-air recording of the ARISS SSTV Series 34 event
  (ISS, 437.550 MHz, Robot36, 2026-10-22). Recorded and contributed by the
  project's own user from their personal archive for regression use; ARISS
  invites reception and decoding of its public SSTV transmissions
  (ariss.org). Decode verified 2026-10-23: full frame, byte-identical to
  the independently produced reference decode, visually inspected.

